* Field purposes (Enter/Edit Names). Names match ENTRIES.FRM.
/*
Chip / timing
-------------
BIB         Printed bib. Chip reads attach to this number. If a runner wore
            the wrong bib, the chip and times at this bib slot are already
            correct -- swap identity fields only.
CHIP        Transponder / chip ID tied to the bib.
GUNSTART    Clock time of the gun. Start of gun elapsed time.
CHIPSTART   Clock time when this chip crossed the start mat. Start of net
            (chip) time. May be unused in gun-only / elite races.
Finish      Clock time when this chip crossed the finish mat.


LPT (Live Predictive Tracking)
------------------------------
Split fields hold the clock time copied from the matching split event by
Events2DB.rsm. @CalcStatus clears them, rewrites them, and treats any one of
them as proof the runner is on course (IN_PROGRESS) even if the start mat
missed them. The LPT listings subtract ChipStart to send elapsed time.

Split1k     1 km mat. First checkpoint. All distances.
Split2k     2 km mat. All distances.
Split5k     5 km mat. 10K and HALF only (not the 5K finish).
Split8k     8 km mat. 10K only.
Split10k    10 km mat. HALF only.
Split18k    18 km mat. HALF only.
Estimated   Estimated finish time from the registration question. Race Roster
            uses it to plot a runner between the start and the first mat,
            which is the only pace it has while they are still STARTING.

A runner is uploaded to Race Roster only if they have a time on some event.
The dummy Status event carries 0 for that purpose; it is listed under the
Hide header so Race Roster does not treat it as a split.


Results
-------
RACE            Distance / sub-event this runner is in. Exact stored values
                differ by template.
RUNNER STATUS   Calculated race-day status sent to Race Roster as Race Status:
                COMPLETE (Finish), IN_PROGRESS (ChipStart or any split, no
                Finish), STARTING (no mat read yet). Recalc with @CalcStatus.
DNF             DNF or DQ flag. Not the same as RUNNER STATUS.
TIME            Elapsed gun time (Finish minus GUNSTART).
NETTIME         Elapsed chip time (Finish minus CHIPSTART).
PACE            Pace derived from elapsed time.
PLACE           Overall place. This template calculates PLACE from chip time
                (@CalcPlaces). May differ from gun-time overall awards.
DIV             Age/gender division code (set from Entries.INI).
DIVPLACE / DIVTOTAL     Place and field size in the division.
SEXPLACE / SEXTOTAL     Place and field size by sex.
AGEPLACE / AGETOTAL     Place and field size in the age group.
Result URL      Public results link (Race Roster).


Personal
--------
Personal runner information: FIRST NAME, LAST NAME, Name, AGE, BIRTHDATE,
SEX, CLUB, ADDRESS, CITY, STATE, ZIP, EMAIL, PHONE, TSHIRT.
*/
